  "question": {
    "text": "A radioactive element gets spilled over the floor of a room. Its half-life period is $30$ days. If the initial activity is ten times the permissible value, after how many days will it be safe to enter the room?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$1000$ days\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$300$ days\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$10$ days\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$100$ days",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Activity $\\left(-\\frac{\\mathrm{dN}}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right) \\propto \\mathrm{N}$\n$\\mathrm{N}=\\mathrm{N}_{\\circ}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{\\mathrm{n}}$\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{N}}{\\mathrm{N}_{\\circ}}=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{\\mathrm{n}}$\n$\\frac{1}{10}=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{\\mathrm{n}} \\Rightarrow 10=2^{\\mathrm{n}}$\n$\\log 10=\\mathrm{nlog} 2$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{n}=\\frac{1}{0.301}=3.32$\n$\\mathrm{t}=\\mathrm{n} \\times \\mathrm{t}_{112}$\n$=3.32 \\times 30=99.6 \\text { days }$\nHence, (D) is correct."
  }
}